From: SM-G955N Ubuntu port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] fbdev: DECON: preserve framebuffer mmap page offsets

DECON's mmap callback discarded every caller offset by passing zero to
dma_buf_mmap. Mapping a later framebuffer page therefore silently aliased the
start, and an out-of-range offset could appear successful at offset zero.
Pass the requested relative page offset to the existing dma-buf mapper.

The pinned dma_buf_mmap checks unsigned page-offset addition overflow and
allocation bounds before calling the exporter. ION also checks its offset and
length and retains its protected-buffer/VM_IO/cache/mapping policy. Keep the
existing write-combine protection; do not turn the display's smem_start DMA
IOVA into a CPU physical address or add it to the offset. Offset-zero mappings
retain their existing behavior. Without ION support, return ENODEV rather than
claim that an unmapped VMA was established.

This fixes the mmap offset/result contract; it neither supplies GPU acceleration
nor establishes that a display restart or the captured MMU fault is resolved.
Based on pinned Samsung and dma-buf source; no live display operation performed.

diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu/decon_dsi.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu/decon_dsi.c
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu/decon_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu/decon_dsi.c
@@ -1025,11 +1025,14 @@
 	struct decon_win *win = info->par;
 	vma->vm_page_prot = pgprot_writecombine(vma->vm_page_prot);
 
-	ret = dma_buf_mmap(win->dma_buf_data[0].dma_buf, vma, 0);
+	/* fb offsets are relative to the framebuffer, in pages. Let dma-buf
+	 * and ION validate the requested offset/length against the allocation.
+	 */
+	ret = dma_buf_mmap(win->dma_buf_data[0].dma_buf, vma, vma->vm_pgoff);
 
 	return ret;
 #else
-	return 0;
+	return -ENODEV;
 #endif
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(decon_mmap);
